_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State explicitly which artifact the shadow comparison uses (planner pre-cap mutation set vs post-cap applied set) and reconcile 'caps before lifecycle intent' with legacy's cap-after-compute partition (_partition_by_mode_cap / _mode_sort_key) so the fail-loud gate compares like-for-like.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0975,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Outcome: 'Run selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limits before any lifecycle or remote effect.'","Step 5: 'Shadow-compare plan mutations/dispositions to legacy output and fail loudly on unexplained divergence in tests.'","apply_planning.py:92-103: legacy computes the full mutation list first, then `cap = MODE_CAPS.get(mode)`, `ordered = sorted(mutations_input, key=_mode_sort_key)`, slice `ordered[:cap]` — caps are applied AFTER compute, not before planning.","AC line 2: 'Selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limits exclude work before any lifecycle intent or remote operation is eligible.'"],"finding":"The plan requires mode caps to run 'before any lifecycle or remote effect' AND requires the shadow planner to compare its mutations/dispositions to legacy output and fail loudly on unexplained divergence, but legacy applies MODE_CAPS AFTER computing the full mutation list (apply_planning._partition_by_mode_cap sorts by _mode_sort_key then slices the first `cap`). The plan does not specify WHICH artifact the shadow compares — the planner's pre-cap mutation set or its post-cap applied set — so a cap-before-plan planner could legitimately emit a different mutation set than legacy's pre-cap list and either trip the fail-loud comparison spuriously or silently mask the reordering.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0f5b5f3d445435fa","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Outcome ('Run selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limits before any lifecycle or remote effect'); Plan step 5; AC line 2 and AC line 5","norm_id":"n967f870724097551","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A bootstrap-strict pass (cap=10) where the planner caps before materializing lifecycle intents but legacy computes all mutations then defers the tail — the shadow sees a smaller emitted set than legacy's pre-cap list.","A pass where _mode_sort_key's outbound-create-first priority changes which items survive the cap, so plan-order and legacy-order disagree on which mutations are 'applied'."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Have the planner emit the full pre-cap mutation/disposition set for the shadow comparison against legacy's pre-cap compute_mutations output, and represent the cap as a separate deterministic partition step that reuses the existing _mode_sort_key ordering — so cap-before-lifecycle-eligibility holds without changing the mutation SET the shadow compares.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","eviden